From d5aef82bdf1c963a5d06016446df5385fcdb32bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pw4-port <pw4-port@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:01:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] binder: replace 4.1's binder with Readom's Oreo binder,
 adapted to 4.1 APIs

The binder in Amazon's 4.1.15 predates Android 8: one /dev/binder, no
scatter-gather, no fd arrays. Android 8.1 needs binder, hwbinder and
vndbinder. Take the driver Readom builds for PW3 (its patches 0001, 0003,
0008, 0900, 0901 applied to the staging binder) and move it to 4.1:

- fd helpers: use __alloc_fd/__fd_install/__close_fd, as 4.1's own binder
  does, instead of the copies of 3.0's fs/file.c internals
- kuid_t for the context manager and sender_euid; task_euid(),
  current_euid(), from_kuid()
- task_active_pid_ns() instead of nsproxy->pid_ns
- three-argument hlist_for_each_entry; map_vm_area() takes the page array
- uapi header goes to include/uapi/linux/android/binder.h
- ANDROID_BINDER_DEVICES added to drivers/android/Kconfig

Compiles; not yet run on a device.
